  "thig15.1:23.4": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Poṭṭhi</i> is unique in Pali, and evidently represents the Sanskrit <i lang='pi' translate='no'>pauṣṭika</i>, a robe used for the tonsure ceremony. Also, the father uses <i lang='pi' translate='no'>ghaṭika</i> (“pot”) rather than the familiar <i lang='pi' translate='no'>patta</i> (“bowl”). ",
  "thig15.1:24.1": "",
  "thig15.1:24.2": "",
  "thig15.1:24.3": "For <i lang='pi' translate='no'>mallaka</i> as “mug” see <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an3.100/en/sujato#4.1'>AN 3.100:4.1</a>. ",
